- guard(b2, n6, v2 = 'Order not needed  proceed') and precedence(b2, n6): Maps the "not needed/proceed" condition to action(n6, "order part from Disuki"), contradicting the source logic where this condition should bypass ordering entirely.
- branch(b2, XOR) with precedence(b2, n6) and precedence(b2, n7): Models ordering and receiving as mutually exclusive paths, whereas the source explicitly sequences them as a single workflow step ("order and receive the part from Disuki").
- guard(b2, n7, v2 = 'Order and receive the part'): Routes the ordering requirement directly to action(n7, "receive part from Disuki"), omitting the mandatory prerequisite action(n6, "order part from Disuki").
- defines(v2, ...) and action(n5, ...): Replaces the source's explicit triggering condition "if they need to record the customer's details" with "do the parts need to be ordered...", altering the documented decision rule.
- actor(a_default, "Default", [...]): Labels the responsible participant as "Default" instead of the explicitly stated "Part Provision Team".